# Environment variables

The service is configured by environment variables only{% if .Worker %}; `server serve`
and `server worker` read the same ones{% end %}. Values are checked at startup, and a
missing required value stops the process with a message that names it.

| Variable | Default | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `APP_ENV` | `development` | Deployment name; `production` refuses unsafe settings |
| `GRPC_ADDR` | `:10000` | gRPC listen address (`serve`) |
| `HTTP_ADDR` | `:8080` | REST and `/livez`, `/readyz` (`serve`) |
| `ADMIN_ADDR` | | Admin port, for example `:9090`: `/readyz` with details, `/version`, `/metrics` (Prometheus), `/debug/pprof/`. Keep it private{% if .Worker %}. The worker serves its probes only here{% end %} |
| `GRPC_REFLECTION` | `false` | gRPC server reflection (authenticated like other methods) |
| `SHUTDOWN_DELAY` | `5s` | Time to keep serving after readiness turns off |
| `SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT` | `30s` | Total graceful shutdown budget |
| `TRUSTED_PROXIES` | | Comma-separated CIDRs of the proxies in front of the service (client IP for rate limits) |
| `ERROR_DOMAIN` | `{% .Name %}` | `ErrorInfo.domain` of API errors |
{%- if .Postgres %}
| `DB_URL` | (required) | `postgres://` URL; TLS is required unless it sets `sslmode` |
| `DB_MAX_CONNS` | max(4, CPUs) | Pool size |
| `DB_STATEMENT_TIMEOUT` | `30s` | Per-statement timeout |
| `DB_MIGRATE_ON_START` | `false` | Apply pending migrations before serving |
{%- else if .MySQL %}
| `DB_URL` | (required) | MySQL DSN, `user:pass@tcp(host:3306)/db`; TLS is required unless it sets `tls` (`tls=false` only for a local database) |
| `DB_MAX_CONNS` | `25` | Maximum open connections |
| `DB_MIGRATE_ON_START` | `false` | Apply pending migrations before serving |
{%- end %}
{%- if .Introspection %}
| `AUTH_INTROSPECTION_URL` | (required) | RFC 7662 introspection endpoint; https only (http for localhost) |
| `AUTH_CLIENT_ID`, `AUTH_CLIENT_SECRET` | (required) | Credentials of this service at the endpoint (secret) |
| `AUTH_AUDIENCE` | (required) | This service's audience (`aud` of the introspection response) |
| `AUTH_ISSUER` | | When set, the `iss` every response must carry |
{%- if .Redis %}
| `AUTH_INTROSPECTION_CACHE_KEY` | (required) | At least 32 random bytes, the same on every instance (secret); authenticates the results shared through Redis |
{%- end %}
{%- else %}
| `AUTH_ISSUER` | (required) | JWT issuer (`iss`) |
| `AUTH_JWKS_URL` | (required) | Issuer key set; https only (http for localhost) |
| `AUTH_AUDIENCE` | (required) | This service's audience (`aud`) |
| `AUTH_TOKEN_TYPES` | | Accepted JWT `typ` values, for example `at+jwt` |
{%- end %}
| `AUTH_DISABLED` | `false` | Turn auth off; refused when `APP_ENV=production` |
{%- if .Redis %}
| `REDIS_ADDRS` | (required) | Comma-separated `host:port`; several addresses select Cluster mode |
| `REDIS_MASTER_NAME` | | Sentinel master name (Sentinel mode) |
| `REDIS_USERNAME`, `REDIS_PASSWORD` | | Redis ACL credentials (secret) |
| `REDIS_DB` | `0` | Database number (single node and Sentinel) |
| `REDIS_TLS` | `true` | TLS to Redis; `false` only for a local Redis |
{%- if .Cache %}
| `CACHE_TTL` | `5m` | How long a cached item is served |
{%- end %}
{%- end %}
{%- if .GCP %}
| `PUBSUB_PROJECT` | (required) | Google Cloud project of the topic and subscription |
| `PUBSUB_EMULATOR_HOST` | | Use the Pub/Sub emulator at this address (local only) |
| `PUBSUB_ITEMS_TOPIC` | `{% .Name %}-items` | Topic of the ItemCreated events |
| `PUBSUB_ITEMS_SUBSCRIPTION` | `{% .Name %}-items-worker` | Subscription the worker consumes |
| `PUBSUB_ORDERED` | `true` | Must match the subscription's message ordering |
| `PUBSUB_MAX_DELIVERY_ATTEMPTS` | `5` | Must match the subscription's dead-letter policy (`0` without one) |
| `PUBSUB_CONCURRENCY` | `10` | Messages the worker handles at once |
{%- else if .Kafka %}
| `PUBSUB_BROKERS` | (required) | Comma-separated seed brokers, `host:port` |
| `PUBSUB_TLS` | `true` | TLS to the brokers; `false` only for a local broker |
| `PUBSUB_ITEMS_TOPIC` | `{% .Name %}-items` | Topic of the ItemCreated events |
| `PUBSUB_ITEMS_SUBSCRIPTION` | `{% .Name %}-items-worker` | Consumer group of the worker |
| `PUBSUB_MAX_DELIVERY_ATTEMPTS` | `5` | Deliveries before a message goes to the dead-letter topic |
| `PUBSUB_ITEMS_DEAD_LETTER_TOPIC` | `{% .Name %}-items.dlq` | Dead-letter topic |
| `PUBSUB_CONCURRENCY` | `10` | Messages the worker handles at once |
{%- else if .SQS %}
| `PUBSUB_ITEMS_TOPIC` | (required) | URL of the queue of the ItemCreated events, which the worker consumes |
| `PUBSUB_CONCURRENCY` | `10` | Messages the worker handles at once |
| `AWS_REGION`, `AWS_*` | | Standard AWS SDK settings and credentials; `AWS_ENDPOINT_URL_SQS` for a local queue |
{%- end %}
{%- if .Jobs %}
| `JOBS_WORKERS` | `10` | Tasks the worker runs at once |
{%- end %}
{%- if .Webhooks %}
| `WEBHOOK_DELIVERY_WORKERS` | `10` | Webhooks the worker sends at once |
| `WEBHOOK_DELIVERY_TIMEOUT` | `15s` | Bound of one delivery attempt |
| `WEBHOOK_DELIVERY_ALLOW_HTTP` | `false` | Accept `http://` endpoints, for local development; refused in production |
{%- end %}
| `RATE_LIMIT_DISABLED` | `false` | Turn rate limits off |
| `RATE_LIMIT_DRY_RUN` | `false` | Count and log, never reject |
| `RATE_LIMIT_EXEMPT` | | Comma-separated `user:<id>`, `ip:<address>` or `ip:<CIDR>` |
| `LOG_LEVEL`, `LOG_FORMAT`, `LOG_SCHEMA`, `LOG_OUTPUT` | `info`, `json`, detected, stdout | See `github.com/dungnh3/kitchen/log` |
| `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT` and other `OTEL_*` | | Traces are exported over OTLP when `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT` (or `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TRACES_ENDPOINT`) is set; metrics also need `OTEL_METRICS_EXPORTER=otlp` |
{%- if .PubSub %}

## Subscriptions

Each consumer added with `zen add consumer` reads its own topic; its
variables start with `PUBSUB_<NAME>_` and are required.

| Variable | Default | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
<!-- zen:subscriptions -->
{%- end %}

## gRPC clients

Each service added with `zen add client` has its own variables, which
start with its name, for example `BILLING_`. Calls use TLS with the system
roots unless `<NAME>_INSECURE=true`.

| Variable | Default | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
<!-- zen:clients -->

## Received webhooks

Each webhook added with `zen add webhook` has its own secret,
`<NAME>_WEBHOOK_SECRET`: the sender's `whsec_` secret or `whpk_` public key
(Standard Webhooks). During a rotation give both, comma-separated.

| Variable | Default | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
<!-- zen:webhooks -->

## Production

- Set `APP_ENV=production`; unsafe settings such as `AUTH_DISABLED` are
  refused there.
- Secrets: {% if .SQL %}`DB_URL` (its password), {% end %}{% if .Redis %}`REDIS_PASSWORD`, {% end %}{% if .Introspection %}`AUTH_CLIENT_SECRET`, {% if .Redis %}`AUTH_INTROSPECTION_CACHE_KEY`, {% end %}{% end %}the `*_WEBHOOK_SECRET` values and the credentials of
  telemetry exporters. Inject them from your secret store; never commit them.
{%- if .SQL %}
- Use a TLS `DB_URL`, and run `server migrate up` as a deploy step with
  `DB_MIGRATE_ON_START=false`.
{%- end %}
{%- if .Redis %}
- Keep `REDIS_TLS=true`.
{%- end %}
{%- if .GCP %}
- Create the topic and the subscription (message ordering on, a dead-letter
  policy) with your infrastructure tool, and keep `PUBSUB_ORDERED` and
  `PUBSUB_MAX_DELIVERY_ATTEMPTS` equal to their settings. The worker needs
  `roles/pubsub.subscriber`, the server `roles/pubsub.publisher`; credentials
  come from Application Default Credentials (Workload Identity).
{%- else if .Kafka %}
- Create the topics, including the dead-letter topic, with your
  infrastructure tool, and keep `PUBSUB_TLS=true`.
{%- else if .SQS %}
- Create the queue with a redrive policy (dead-letter queue), and grant the
  worker `sqs:ReceiveMessage`, `sqs:DeleteMessage`,
  `sqs:ChangeMessageVisibility` and `sqs:GetQueueAttributes`, the server
  `sqs:SendMessage`.
{%- end %}
- Set `TRUSTED_PROXIES` to the CIDRs of your load balancer, and keep
  `ADMIN_ADDR` off the public network.
